  data:  # 7ba4
    kind: work_item  # 7ba4
    title: "cpp: an in-class constructor or member template is emitted as a free function with an unqualified name, and members of a class with a qualified name (class X::Impl) stay unqualified"  # 7ba4
    status: todo_hard  # 7ba4
    priority: 3  # 7ba4
    parent:  # 7ba4
    tags:  # 7ba4
    - cpp  # 7ba4
    - analysis_quality  # 7ba4
    isbefore: []  # 7ba4
    duplicate_of: []  # 7ba4
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7ba4
    pr_ref:  # 7ba4
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 while fixing WI-saduj (read in code and on fixtures; not measured on a corpus).\n\ncpp's _extract_symbols_from_tree decides a definition's kind and qualified name from the LEAF type of its declarator plus `_get_enclosing_class`. Three in-class shapes come out as a free function, or unqualified:\n  1. An in-class constructor `struct S { S() {..} };` -- leaf `identifier` -> kind=function, name `S` (not method `S::S`; an out-of-class `S::S()` is method `S::S`).\n  2. An in-class member template `struct T { template <typename U> U* get() {..} };` -- inside a template_declaration the leaf is `identifier`, not `field_identifier` -> kind=function, name `get`. Seen on sherpa-onnx: `template <typename Manager> void InitKeywords(Manager *mgr)` in KeywordSpotterTransducerImpl is function `InitKeywords` while its sibling overloads are method `KeywordSpotterTransducerImpl::InitKeywords`.\n  3. A member of a class whose own name is qualified (`class OfflineX::Impl {..}`): `_get_enclosing_class` reads only a direct `type_identifier`, so the method stays unqualified (sherpa-onnx: ten `~Impl` destructors, all method `~Impl`).\nEffect: same-class path_hint preference and the containment linker see a free function; the in-class and out-of-class spellings of one member get different names. WI-saduj added `_cpp_in_class_body` (parent is field_declaration_list, through a template_declaration) for operator/destructor/template leaves only; using it for `identifier` leaves too would cover 1 and 2, but it changes kind and name for existing symbols, so measure first (stable_id and edge-id churn)."  # 7ba4
    fields: {}  # 7ba4
- op: discuss  # b315
