  clock: 2  # b315
  nonce: b315  # b315
  message: "Bears on WI-hilum (branch jgstern-agent/fix/hilum): cpp overload choice re-chooses a call among definitions with the picked symbol's EXACT name. A member template defined in a class body (sherpa-onnx keyword-spotter-transducer-impl.h L319 template InitKeywords(Manager *mgr)) is named unqualified 'InitKeywords' with kind function, so it is outside the 'KeywordSpotterTransducerImpl::InitKeywords' overload set. Two consequences, measured on sherpa-onnx d7526c8: (1) the call InitKeywords(is) at L336, inside that template, still binds the template itself (a self-call the hilum fix cannot see); (2) the L300/L314 calls now resolve uniquely to the istream& overload only BECAUSE the template is missing from the set -- once this item qualifies member templates, those calls become an ambiguous record {L283, L319} (both take one argument) unless an argument-shape check (object vs pointer) separates them. Re-measure the InitKeywords sites when this lands."  # b315
